---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Arrow from '../../components/Arrow.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Journal | Parts Relay"
  description="Read field notes on sourcing parts, including missing kit items, worn reference labels and choosing the right assembly."
>
  <div class="lib-page lib-journal" data-lib-list>
    <div class="lib-bound">
      <header class="lib-journal-intro">
        <h1 tabindex="-1">Journal</h1>
        <p>
          A few questions that come up at the parts counter, from what’s in the box to what you can
          still read on the old unit.
        </p>
      </header>
      <div class="lib-controls">
        <div class="lib-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Filter by topic">
          <button type="button" data-lib-filter="All" aria-pressed="true">
            All
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-lib-filter="Repair shops" aria-pressed="false">
            Repair shops
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-lib-filter="Distributor counter" aria-pressed="false">
            Distributor counter
          </button>
          <button type="button" data-lib-filter="Parts identification" aria-pressed="false">
            Parts identification
          </button>
        </div>
        <label class="lib-search">
          <svg
            aria-hidden="true"
            viewBox="0 0 24 24"
            fill="none"
            stroke="currentColor"
            stroke-width="1.55"
            stroke-linecap="round"
            stroke-linejoin="round"
          >
            <circle cx="10.5" cy="10.5" r="6.5" />
            <path d="m16 16 5 5" />
          </svg>
          <span class="lib-visually-hidden">Search articles</span>
          <input type="search" placeholder="Search…" autocomplete="off" data-lib-search />
        </label>
      </div>
      <ul class="lib-story-grid" data-lib-results>
        <li data-lib-item data-lib-topic="Repair shops">
          <a class="lib-story-card" href="/journal/brake-pad-sets/">
            <div
              class="lib-art lib-art-pads"
              aria-label="Illustration of a brake disc and separated pad set"
              role="img"
            >
              <span>Front axle</span>
              <img src="/assets/brake-pads.svg" alt="" />
              <b>PAD SET</b>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h2>The missing wear sensor</h2>
              <p>
                A front pad set has a catalogue number. Its wear sensor might need a line of its own
                on the quote.
              </p>
              <small>Repair shops, 3 min read</small>
            </div>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li data-lib-item data-lib-topic="Distributor counter">
          <a class="lib-story-card" href="/journal/alternator-labels/">
            <div
              class="lib-art lib-art-alt"
              aria-label="Technical illustration of an alternator"
              role="img"
            >
              <span>Electrical</span>
              <img src="/assets/alternator.svg" alt="" />
              <b>ALTERNATOR</b>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h2>When the alternator number has worn away</h2>
              <p>
                The rating on the old unit is legible. The end of the part number has rubbed off.
                What can the shop tell the counter?
              </p>
              <small>Distributor counter, 3 min read</small>
            </div>
          </a>
        </li>
        <li data-lib-item data-lib-topic="Parts identification">
          <a class="lib-story-card" href="/journal/mirror-glass/">
            <div
              class="lib-art lib-art-mirror"
              aria-label="Editorial illustration of the glass separated from a left mirror"
              role="img"
            >
              <span>Bodywork</span>
              <i class="lib-shell-shape"></i>
              <i class="lib-glass-shape"></i>
              <b>MIRROR GLASS</b>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h2>Before you quote a door mirror</h2>
              <p>
                A crack in heated glass and a broken mounting base send the counter to different
                places in the drawing.
              </p>
              <small>Parts identification, 3 min read</small>
            </div>
          </a>
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p class="lib-visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" data-lib-count></p>
      <div class="lib-empty" data-lib-empty hidden>
        <h2>No articles found</h2>
        <p>Try a part name such as alternator, or clear your filters to see every story.</p>
        <button type="button" data-lib-reset>
          Clear filters
        </button>
      </div>
      <section class="lib-desk-note">
        <div>
          <h2>What to get in writing on a quote</h2>
          <p>
            A supplier may offer an alternative to the part you asked about. Before you give the
            workshop a collection time, find out exactly which item the offer covers.
          </p>
        </div>
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>Which reference?</dt>
            <dd>
              Write the supplier’s number beside the vehicle and fitting position. If their
              catalogue lists two versions, ask what distinguishes the one they’ve quoted.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>What comes with it?</dt>
            <dd>
              Get a separate line for any hardware the technician needs to buy. A quote for a kit
              should say what’s inside.
            </dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>When can the shop get it?</dt>
            <dd>
              Confirm price, available quantity and collection or delivery time for each quoted
              reference. A substitute can have a different lead time.
            </dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <a class="lib-inline-link" href="/workshops/fit-check/">
          Try the fit-check exercise
          <Arrow />
        </a>
        <p class="lib-product-note">
          Longer read:
          <a class="lib-inline-link" href="/guides/counter/">
            the headlamp that still works with a broken mounting tab
          </a>
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  import '../../scripts/library.js';
</script>
